cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CGE-Core, please cite it as below. Also cite the original PyCGE
  (Fung & Burtwistle, NIST) and the relevant underlying model sources: Hosoe,
  Gasawa & Hashimoto (2010), the separately obtained IFPRI Standard CGE
  documentation and source package, or Condon, Dahl & Devarajan (1987) for the
  CAMCGE replication. See README.md ("Provenance and license") for details.
title: "CGE-Core: a Pyomo-based computable general equilibrium framework"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Miraflor
    given-names: James Matthew
    email: jbmiraflor@up.edu.ph
    affiliation: "Scientific Computing Laboratory, Department of Computer Science, University of the Philippines Diliman"
version: 0.6.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/miraflor/CGE-core"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - cge
  - computable-general-equilibrium
  - pyomo
  - economics
  - policy-simulation
abstract: >-
  CGE-Core is a corrected and substantially revised fork of PyCGE by Juan Fung
  and Charley Burtwistle (U.S. National Institute of Standards and Technology,
  2017; public domain under 17 U.S.C. 105). The inherited PyCGE code and Hosoe
  model ports are not James Matthew Miraflor's original work. He directed and
  reviewed an AI-assisted process covering the fork's corrections, engine API,
  testing, documentation, IFPRI implementation, CAMCGE replication benchmark,
  and release workflow. He is cited as project lead and maintainer of this
  revised software project, not as author of the underlying models or
  inherited code. The official IFPRI source package and test data remain
  external. Hosoe is checked
  against GAMS Model Library references, IFPRI against full-precision external
  reference runs, and CAMCGE against its published base equilibrium and three
  policy experiments.
references:
